{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_empty_array_trap", "label": "The empty-array trap", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A parent with no children should return []. The naked aggregate returns [null]; FILTER alone returns null. Getting [] takes FILTER plus coalesce."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_left_join_null_row", "label": "LEFT JOIN NULL row kept by array_agg", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "LEFT JOIN invents a childless parent row with NULL child columns. array_agg and jsonb_agg keep NULLs, so the client sees [null] and length 1."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_filter_empty_group_null", "label": "FILTER empty group is NULL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FILTER (WHERE child.id IS NOT NULL) removes the fake row, leaving an empty group. Every aggregate over an empty input is NULL \u2014 same rule as sum over no rows."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_child_collection_idiom", "label": "Canonical child-collection idiom", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object(...) ORDER BY k) FILTER (WHERE id IS NOT NULL), '[]'::jsonb). Four parts: build_object, ORDER BY, FILTER, coalesce. '{}' is the empty PostgreSQL array, not a JSON array."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_lateral_nested_payload", "label": "Two-level LATERAL nested payload", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "LEFT JOIN LATERAL \u2026 ON true nests inner GROUP BY so each order aggregates its items before the outer aggregate collects orders. Flat dual joins multiply fan-out."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_shape_in_sql_vs_js", "label": "Shape in SQL versus stitch in JS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shape in SQL when nesting is fixed and child sets are small \u2014 one round trip, atomic, untyped. Stitch in JS when pieces are needed separately or children need pagination. Either beats N+1. Measured 292 vs 580 bytes."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_empty_array_trap", "target": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_left_join_null_row", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-6-aggregation/05-json-agg/03-the-empty-array-trap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_6_aggregation_05_json_agg_03_the_empty_array_trap_left_join_null_row", "target": 